BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-180909@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260428T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T183000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Atlantic's Nick Thompson 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\
 nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180909\n\n5:00PM Recep
 tion\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into a wide-ranging conversation with Nic
 holas Thompson\, CEO of The Atlantic. During his tenure\, the publication
  has won the National Magazine Award for General Excellence three times\, 
 become one of the fastest-growing news organizations in the country\, and 
 reached record profitability and subscriber growth in its 157-year history
 . He is also the author of the national bestseller The Running Ground an
 d host of the podcast The Most Interesting Thing in AI\, where he explore
 s the rapidly evolving world of artificial intelligence.\n\nThompson will 
 be joined in conversation by Claire Hughes Johnson\, a technology leader a
 nd former Chief Operating Officer of Stripe. Together\, they will explore
  the forces shaping today’s media and technology landscapes - from the f
 uture of AI and innovation to the evolving role of storytelling and leader
 ship in a rapidly changing world.\n\n*This event is complimentary and rese
 rved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180909
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-180910@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260429T130000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T150000
SUMMARY:90 Minutes of Innovation: Networks\, Intelligence & the Future of D
 ecision-Making 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\
 nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180910\n\n1:00PM Progr
 am\, 2:30PM Networking\nWhat can we learn from the individuals shaping AI\
 , enterprise transformation\, and modern engineering at the highest levels
 ?\n\nIn the latest edition of 90 Minutes of Innovation\, John Werner - ven
 ture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI columnist - will lead a ser
 ies of one-on-one conversations with three remarkable leaders\, each offer
 ing a distinct perspective on innovation\, leadership\, and the moment we�
 ��re in.\n\nJon Hirschtick\, founder of SolidWorks and Onshape\, is a pion
 eering force in computer-aided design who has transformed how engineers an
 d designers build the world. An MIT alumnus\, he used winnings from the In
 stitute’s legendary blackjack team to launch his first company - an expe
 rience that later inspired the film 21.\n\nSandy Pentland\, MIT professor 
 with appointments at MIT and Stanford\, and one of the most cited data sci
 entists globally\, whose work on human behavior\, social networks\, and �
 �reality mining” has fundamentally reshaped how we understand trust\, ci
 ties\, and collective intelligence. He will speak on his recent book\, Sh
 ared Wisdom: Cultural Evolution in the Age of AI.\n\nDavid Kenny\, Executi
 ve Chairman of Nielsen and former CEO of IBM Watson\, with prior leadershi
 p roles at Akamai and The Weather Channel\, has operated at the forefront 
 of AI\, data\, and global enterprise transformation.\n\nThrough individual
  interviews\, the afternoon will explore their personal journeys\, the ide
 as that have defined their work\, and how each sees the rapidly evolving l
 andscape of AI\, technology\, and innovation today. Expect an engaging\, i
 nsight-rich experience that connects lived experience with forward-looking
  perspective - offering a rare window into how these leaders think\, build
 \, and lead.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only
 . Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/180910
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
