BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-182103@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260512T130000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T150000
SUMMARY:Hands-On Impact: Household Goods
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist On
 ly\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182103\n\nA simple 
 set of kitchen tools can be the difference between a space and a home.\n\n
 Join The ‘Quin Impact Fund for a hands-on volunteer experience in partne
 rship with Household Goods\, where you will assemble Kitchen Starter Sets 
 for individuals and families transitioning into stable housing. Together\,
  you will unpack\, sort\, and thoughtfully build essential kits - each one
  filled with everyday items that make it possible to cook\, gather\, and b
 egin again.\n\nHousehold Goods furnishes more than 2\,500 homes each year\
 , yet the demand for basic kitchen essentials remains constant. These star
 ter sets - simple\, practical\, and deeply impactful - help ensure that ev
 ery home begins with the tools needed for daily life.\n\nMembers are invit
 ed to contribute by donating new or gently used kitchen items or supportin
 g purchases through a curated Amazon wish list ahead of the event. A meani
 ngful opportunity to give back\, connect\, and play a small part in helpin
 g someone build a home from the ground up.\n\n*This event is complimentary
  and reserved for members only. For any questions regarding donation item
 s\, please contact The ‘Quin Impact Fund team at impact@thequin.com.\n\
 nShop the Amazon Wishlist here.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182103
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-182250@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260512T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T190000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: AI Powered Women
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182250\n\n5:30PM Reception
 \, 6:00PM Discussion\nAI is reshaping the world - but who is shaping AI?\n
 \nThis discussion brings together leading women at the forefront of artifi
 cial intelligence to explore the human decisions\, ethical frameworks\, an
 d leadership required to guide this moment of rapid transformation.\n\nDr.
  Felicia Newhouse\, founder of AI-Powered Women—a global learning platfo
 rm and 1\,200-person MIT summit focused on building the workforce infrastr
 ucture behind responsible AI adoption—will share insights on how organiz
 ations translate AI investment into real-world implementation\, where lead
 ership\, culture\, and human capability determine success. She is joined b
 y Dr. Karrie Karahalios of the MIT Media Lab\, a pioneer in algorithmic ac
 countability\, and Dr. Cansu Canca\, Director of Responsible AI Practice a
 t Northeastern University and founder of AI Ethics Lab and creator of Puz
 zle-solving in Ethics (PiE) Model.\n\nTogether\, they will examine how AI 
 systems reflect the values and assumptions of those who build and deploy t
 hem and why diverse leadership is not just important\, but essential. From
  bias and governance to trust\, identity\, and decision-making\, the conve
 rsation moves beyond technology to the deeper question of responsibility.\
 n\nAn intimate\, interdisciplinary conversation on women shaping the futur
 e of AI and the systems that will shape us all.\n\n*This event is complime
 ntary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will be 
 served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/182250
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-176385@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260514T173000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260514
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260517
SUMMARY:Twin Farms Takeover
LOCATION:Café Q
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 5:30 PM – 10 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.co
 m/events/176385\n\nExperience the refined elegance of Twin Farms this May 
 as Café Q welcomes the celebrated culinary team from the two Michelin key
  Vermont resort for an exclusive three-day takeover.\n\nLed by Executive C
 hef Nathan Rich—recognized for his innovative approach to luxury dining 
 and commitment to seasonal\, locally sourced ingredients—alongside Chef 
 Sylvain Courbet\, whose Alpine roots and global culinary journey inform hi
 s thoughtful\, ingredient-driven cuisine\, this special residency brings t
 he spirit of Twin Farms to The ‘Quin House.\n\nThroughout the collaborat
 ion\, members are invited to experience Twin Farms across multiple moments
  of the day. Breakfast and lunch will feature a selection of thoughtfully 
 composed specials\, offering a preview of the chefs’ seasonal approach\,
  while dinner will transform Café Q into a full Twin Farms takeover—sho
 wcasing a complete menu designed to highlight the very best of spring.\n\n
 Begin your evening with vibrant starters such as Lobster Tacos with Ossetr
 a caviar\, Green Gazpacho with avocado and spring peas\, or Cavatelli with
  morel mushrooms and ramp butter. Entrées highlight refined\, ingredient-
 forward dishes including Vermont Wagyu Striploin\, Truffled Chicken\, Icel
 andic Cod with lobster cream\, and Curried Cauliflower with saffron broth.
  Conclude with elegant desserts like Vermont Ricotta Beignets with maple c
 ream or a decadent Three Chocolate Pavé.\n\nRooted in the rich agricultur
 al traditions of Vermont and inspired by global technique\, each dish refl
 ects Twin Farms’ dedication to craftsmanship\, storytelling\, and an imm
 ersive dining experience.\n\nDuring dinner service\, Café Q’s regular m
 enu will be set aside\, allowing this one-of-a-kind culinary experience to
  take center stage.\n\nMake a Reservation.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/176385
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
